<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The autogenerative thesis did not arise ex nihilo.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Its intellectual lineage is a braid of four strands:</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\begin</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">Thermodynamic epistemology</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} (Boltzmann 1877; Jaynes 1957; Friston 2010)  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">   Cognition as variational free-energy minimization.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">Statistical learning</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} (Shannon 1948; Cover </span><span style="color: rgb(215, 186, 125);">\&amp;</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> Thomas 1991)  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">   Language as a channel whose codebook is the corpus.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">Geometric information theory</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} (Amari 1985; Ay 2015)  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">   Conditional distributions form a Riemannian manifold.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\item</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);"> \emph</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230); font-style: italic;">Non-Markovian natural computation</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">} (Barenholtz 2025)  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">   Trajectories, not states, are the primitive.</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\end</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">enumerate</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Peirceâ€™s triadic sign (1893) prefigures the syntaxâ€“semanticsâ€“embodiment bundle; Piagetâ€™s equilibration (1952) anticipates the fixed-point law </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\nabla</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);"> R=</span><span style="color: rgb(181, 206, 168);">0</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">What is new is the synthesis: a single differential structure whose geodesics are thoughts, whose attractor is understanding, and whose equilibrium projector is automation.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">The departure from classical AI is categorical.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Symbolic systems impose external grammars; connectionist systems impose fixed Markov windows.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Autogenerative systems impose nothingâ€”they learn the manifold that learns itself.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
