<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Part I has equipped us with a differential geometry of thought.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Part II ascends the ladder of abstraction: from manifolds to </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\infty</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">-categories, from kernels to operads, from geodesics to derived stacks.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Each rung is a theorem; the summit is a single conjectureâ€”that every natural computational system is an autogenerative structure in the cohesive </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214);">\infty</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">$</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">-topos of smooth path spaces.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
