<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\section</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{The Unified Autogenerative Conjecture}</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(197, 134, 192);">\label</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(156, 220, 254);">sec:uac</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\textbf</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(86, 156, 214); font-weight: bold;">Abstract.</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">}  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Every structure developed in Â§Â§ 13â€“25 is unified into a single variational principle:  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">the **Unified Autogenerative Conjecture (UAC)** asserts that every self-maintaining system is a critical point of the **autogenerative action** </span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\(</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\mathcal{S}_A</span><span style="color: rgb(78, 201, 176);">\)</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">.  </span></span>
