<span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">To exist is to learn. This work aims to show that learning, at every level of the universe, is the process by which curvature maintains itselfâ€” the autogenerative equilibrium we call understanding.'' \end{minipage} \end{center} \vspace*{\fill} &nbsp; \clearpage \tableofcontents &nbsp; %====================================================================== % END FRONTMATTER %======================================================================% ============================================================ % part1_autogenerative_thesis.tex % Part I â€” The Autogenerative Thesis: From Non-Markovian Language to Cognitive Geometry % ============================================================ &nbsp; \documentclass[12pt,a4paper]{article} &nbsp; % --------------------- Preamble --------------------- \usepackage{fontspec} \setmainfont{TeX Gyre Termes} \usepackage{microtype} \usepackage{geometry} \geometry{margin=1.1in} \usepackage{setspace} \setstretch{1.2} \usepackage{parskip} \usepackage{titlesec} \titleformat{\section}{\Large\bfseries}{\thesection.}{0.8em}{} \titleformat{\subsection}{\large\bfseries}{\thesubsection}{0.6em}{} \titleformat{\paragraph}[runin]{\bfseries}{\theparagraph}{0.8em}{}[.] &nbsp; \usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm,bm} \usepackage{hyperref} \usepackage{enumitem} &nbsp; \begin{document} &nbsp; \begin{center} {\LARGE\bfseries Part I --- The Autogenerative Thesis:\\From Non-Markovian Language to Cognitive Geometry}\\[1em] {\large Flyxion Research Group}\\[1em] \end{center} &nbsp; % ============================================================ \section{Introduction: The Autogenerative Hypothesis} % ============================================================ &nbsp; Language, cognition, and natural computation exhibit an intrinsic property of \emph{autogeneration}: each moment of activity encodes the conditions for its own continuation. The concept, articulated by Barenholtz~(2025), redefines autoregression as more than a statistical convenience; it is the very mode of natural self-propagation. In contrast to Markovian processes, where the next state depends only on the current one, autogenerative systems draw upon the entire trajectory of prior states. They are inherently \emph{non-Markovian}, operating on the accumulated curvature of experience rather than on instantaneous state vectors. &nbsp; This view renders the corpus of language not merely as data but as a \emph{field of continuation rules}â€”a statistical manifold whose internal topology determines its own dynamics. In such a manifold, the </span>pregnant present'' is a boundary condition that enfolds its history and projects its own future trajectory. Autogeneration therefore serves as the bridge between memory, inference, and meaning. The goal of this section is to formalize that bridge using information geometry, category theory, and dynamical-systems analysis.
&nbsp;
