Via the Koopman representation (Â§ 16), restriction maps become conditional expectations $$ E_V^U(A)=\mathbb{E}[A|V] $$; gluing corresponds to enforcing consistency among these expectations.
Hence the operator-algebraic and sheaf-theoretic pictures are dual perspectives on contextual coherence.
