<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">{</span><span style="color: rgb(220, 220, 170);">\large\bfseries</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"> How can understanding itselfâ€”an act of coherence across time, sense, and scaleâ€”be described by a single physical and mathematical law?}</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">This 200-page monograph answers the question with a unified geometric, categorical, and quantum theory of **autogenerative systems**â€”self-maintaining processes that recursively generate their own continuation while preserving informational curvature.</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Part I derives cognition as a non-Markovian autoregressive flow on a Fisherâ€“Rao manifold whose equilibrium defines comprehension as minimal epistemic work.  </span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color: rgb(230, 230, 230);">Part II reformulates learning as adjoint functorial transformation, contextual coherence via sheaf cohomology, and abstraction as renormalization across scales.  </span></span>
